\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 21): PROVED reflection_positivity_reorganization (Step 4b of Lemma 5) + integral_matrix_element_trivial_projection. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"75\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 22): PROVED character_times_matrix_element_integral + triple_product_character_matrix_integral_timelike. Time-like triple product WITHOUT conjugation. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs). See §8.11.27.\",\"id\":\"77\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 23): ANALYZED character-level approach (§8.11.28) — does NOT directly work. KEY FINDINGS: (1) fullReflectReindex w* gives kernel |Φ_w⟩⟨Φ_{w*}| (NOT rank-1 same-vector), (2) σ twist breaks Mercer-PD structure (delta function δ(V⁰,σ(U⁰)) is discontinuous), (3) PD property of exp(-β·S_int) doesn't help because h factors break the quadratic form. CONCLUSION: L² expansion is NECESSARY. Documented in §8.11.29. Build unchanged (GREEN, 2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"76\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 24): PROVED transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect (Step 1 of Lemma 5 Step 4a). Combines Step 4e + Lemma 3 to give fullReflect form: Complex.ofReal(∫ψ·Tψ) = C·∑_w F(w)·∫ Ψ_w·A_w·A_{w*}(σ) dμ⁰. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). Also did DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization challenge (§8.11.30): c^w·c^{w*} does NOT factor as d(x)·conj(d(y)) because c^w couples i(in x) with j(in y); c^{w*}≠conj(c^w) because fullReflectReindex involves link reflection φ with selective dual; fullReflectReindex is NOT a bijection (projection losing w|_positive). Time-like case gives Tr(P^T·B_a·Q^T·B_a†) which is ≥0 iff Q=conj(P).\",\"id\":\"78\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"IN PROGRESS: Lemma 5 Step 4a — L² expansion approach. REMAINING STEPS: (2) Design L² expansion hypothesis, (3) Fubini factorization, (4) Per-link triple product evaluation (BOTH PROVEN), (5) REORGANIZATION (KEY OBSTACLE — c^w·c^{w*} doesn't factor as d(x)·conj(d(y)); see §8.11.30-31 for analysis), (6) Apply reflection_positivity_reorganization, (7) Assemble with integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg. See §8.11.30-31 for full analysis.\",\"id\":\"79\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 25): DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization (§8.11.31). KEY FINDINGS: (1) Reorganization CANNOT be done term-by-term — requires sum over w. (2) PD property of K alone does NOT imply ∫f(g)·f(g⁻¹)·K(g)≥0 — the single integral is NOT the standard PD quadratic form ∫∫f(x)·conj(f(y))·K(x⁻¹y). (3) For single time-like link, per-λ integral is NOT ≥0 (it's an inner product ⟨R,Q⟩, not a norm squared). (4) Sum over σ gives Gram matrix (PSD), but full expression couples different Fourier coefficients F_w,F_u. (5) Even/odd decomposition: I=(1/4)(∫h²·K−∫k²·K) where h=f+f∘θ (even), k=f−f∘θ (odd). (6) Non-negativity is a DEEP property requiring product structure of Boltzmann factor + support of f. (7) c^{w*}≠conj(c^w) is fundamental — σ twist breaks conjugation. MOST PROMISING ALTERNATIVE: plaquette-by-plaquette induction (approach 4) might avoid reorganization obstacle entirely. Build unchanged (GREEN, 2891 jobs).\",\"id\":\"80\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"PENDING: Assemble lemma 6 — close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (axiom count 6→5). See §8.8. Requires Lemma 5 Step 4a (item 79).\",\"id\":\"48\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}","name":"project_task_list"},"id":"8e6884d5-34c4-4381-8a57-18aa6620b91d","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":1548,"turn":0,"is_prune_marker":false}
