{"id":22,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 2559 lines, 150137 bytes --\n2300 |   calc\n2301 |     ∑ p : PlaquetteIndex T L, f p = ∑ p : PlaquetteIndex T L, f (e p) := by\n2302 |       symm\n2303 |       exact Fintype.sum_equiv e (λ p => f (e p)) f (λ p => rfl)\n2304 |     _ = ∑ p : PlaquetteIndex T L, g p := by\n2305 |       refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (λ p hp => ?_)\n2306 |       rw [h_eq p]\n2307 | /-- The Osterwalder-Seiler \"G\" function: the Boltzmann factor for the positive\n2308 | half-lattice, including the interface action at half weight.  This is the\n2309 | function whose integral `∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀` must be shown non-negative. -/\n2310 | noncomputable def osG (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n2311 |     (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ)\n2312 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n2313 |   f U * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U) *\n2314 |   Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U / 2)\n2315 | \n2316 | /-- **Axiom (Transfer-matrix positivity).**\n2317 | \n2318 | For `f` depending only on positive-time and interface links, the integral\n2319 | `∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀ ≥ 0`, where `G = osG` is the Osterwalder-Seiler Boltzmann\n2320 | factor and `θ` is the time-reflection.\n2321 | \n2322 | This is the positivity of the transfer matrix `T` constructed from the\n2323 | plaquette Boltzmann factor.  The mathematical justification is:\n2324 | \n2325 | 1. The plaquette Boltzmann factor `exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃g₄))` is a\n2326 |    positive-definite function on `SU(N)⁴` — this is proved (from the\n2327 |    Peter-Weyl / Clebsch-Gordan axiom) in `PeterWeyl.lean` as\n2328 |    `plaquetteBoltzmannPD`.\n2329 | 2. Positive-definiteness of the plaquette factor implies that the transfer\n2330 |    matrix `T` (which integrates out the negative-time links with the\n2331 |    reflection kernel) is a positive operator on `L²(SU(N)^{interface})`.\n2332 | 3. The identity `∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀ = ∫ g(u)·(Tg)(u) dμ⁺⁰` (proved in\n2333 |    `TransferMatrix.lean` as `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`) then gives\n2334 |    `∫ G·G(θU) ≥ 0` from the positivity of `T`.\n2335 | \n2336 | Steps 2–3 require the full transfer-matrix construction (measure-theoretic\n2337 | factorization of the product Haar measure, Fubini, and the character-expansion\n2338 | argument).  The positive-definiteness of the plaquette factor (step 1) is the\n2339 | key input and is proved in `PeterWeyl.lean`; the remaining measure theory is\n2340 | axiomatized here.  See `docs/found_issues.md` §3 and `docs/gap_analysis.md`. -/\n2341 | axiom transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n2342 |     (hT : Odd T) (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ)\n2343 |     (hf_supported : dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f) :\n2344 |     0 ≤ ∫ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L)\n2345 |         (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2346 |       osG N T L β f\n2347 |         (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L)\n2348 |           (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n2349 |       osG N T L β f\n2350 |         (reflectLinkVariable N\n2351 |           (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L)\n2352 |             (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n2353 |       ∂ productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L)\n2354 |         (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n2355 | \n2356 | lemma gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n2357 |     (hT : Odd T) (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ)\n2358 |     (hf_supported : dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f) :\n2359 |     0 ≤ gibbsExpectation N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n2360 |       (λ U => f U * reflectObservable N f U) := by\n2361 |   dsimp [gibbsExpectation]\n2362 |   have hZ_pos : partitionFunctionFinite N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) > 0 :=\n2363 |     partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n2364 |   refine div_nonneg ?_ (le_of_lt hZ_pos)\n2365 |   set μ₀ := productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) with hμ₀\n2366 |   set S_total := wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) with hS\n2367 |   set U_ext := extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) with hU\n2368 |   have h_total_decomp : ∀ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2369 |       S_total cfg = wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (U_ext cfg) +\n2370 |         wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β (U_ext cfg) +\n2371 |         wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) := by\n2372 |     intro cfg\n2373 |     calc\n2374 |       S_total cfg = wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) (U_ext cfg) := rfl\n2375 |       _ = wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (U_ext cfg) +\n2376 |           wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β (U_ext cfg) +\n2377 |           wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) :=\n2378 |         total_decomposition_os_periodic N T L β (U_ext cfg)\n2379 |   have h_neg_reflect : ∀ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2380 |       wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β (U_ext cfg) =\n2381 |       wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) := by\n2382 |     intro cfg\n2383 |     exact neg_action_reflection_os_periodic N T L β hT (U_ext cfg)\n2384 |   have h_int_reflect : ∀ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2385 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) =\n2386 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) := by\n2387 |     intro cfg\n2388 |     exact interface_action_reflection_symmetric_os_periodic N T L β hT (U_ext cfg)\n2389 |   have h_factorization : ∀ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2390 |       Real.exp (-β * S_total cfg) = \n2391 |       (Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (U_ext cfg)) *\n2392 |         Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2)) *\n2393 |       (Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg))) *\n2394 |         Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) / 2)) := by\n2395 |     intro cfg\n2396 |     rw [h_total_decomp cfg]\n2397 |     have h_mul : -β * (wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (U_ext cfg) + wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β (U_ext cfg) +\n2398 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg)) = \n2399 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (U_ext cfg)) + \n2400 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β (U_ext cfg)) + \n2401 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg)) := by ring\n2402 |     rw [h_mul]\n2403 |     rw [Real.exp_add, Real.exp_add]\n2404 |     rw [h_neg_reflect cfg, h_int_reflect cfg]\n2405 |     have h_exp_split : Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg)) =\n2406 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2) *\n2407 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2) := by\n2408 |       calc\n2409 |         Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg)) =\n2410 |           Real.exp ((-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2) +\n2411 |                    (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2)) := by ring\n2412 |         _ = Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2) *\n2413 |             Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (U_ext cfg) / 2) := by rw [Real.exp_add]\n2414 |     rw [h_exp_split]\n2415 |     ring\n2416 |   set G := osG N T L β f with hG\n2417 |   have h_integrand_eq : ∀ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2418 |       f (U_ext cfg) * f (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) *\n2419 |       Real.exp (-β * S_total cfg) =\n2420 |       G (U_ext cfg) * G (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) := by\n2421 |     intro cfg\n2422 |     dsimp [G, osG]\n2423 |     rw [h_factorization cfg]\n2424 |     ring\n2425 |   have h_fun_eq : (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n2426 |       f (U_ext cfg) * f (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) * Real.exp (-β * S_total cfg)) =\n2427 |     (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n2428 |       G (U_ext cfg) * G (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg))) := by\n2429 |     ext cfg; exact h_integrand_eq cfg\n2430 |   calc\n2431 |     (∫ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2432 |       f (U_ext cfg) * f (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) * Real.exp (-β * S_total cfg) ∂ μ₀)\n2433 |         = (∫ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n2434 |       G (U_ext cfg) * G (reflectLinkVariable N (U_ext cfg)) ∂ μ₀) := by\n2435 |       rw [h_fun_eq]\n2436 |     _ ≥ 0 := by\n2437 |       -- GOAL: Prove that ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) ≥ 0.\n2438 |       -- The positivity follows from `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`, which is\n2439 |       -- justified by `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` (Peter-Weyl / Clebsch-Gordan) ⟹\n2440 |       -- transfer matrix T positive ⟹ ∫ G·G(θU) ≥ 0.  See the axiom's docstring.\n2441 |       exact transferMatrixPositivity_axiom N T L β hT f hf_supported\n2442 | \n2443 | /-! ## Clean factorization and the PD-structure obstruction\n2444 | \n2445 | The reflection-positivity integrand `osG(U) · osG(θU)` factorizes cleanly as\n2446 | `f(U) · f(θU) · exp(-β S_W(U))` (lemma `osG_thetaG_factorization` below).\n2447 | This shows that the axiom `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` is equivalent to:\n2448 | \n2449 |     ∫ f(U) · f(θU) · exp(-β S_W(U)) dμ₀ ≥ 0\n2450 | \n2451 | where `exp(-β S_W)` is the full Boltzmann factor, proved positive-definite on the\n2452 | full link-variable group by `boltzmannFactorPD` (in `BoltzmannFactor.lean`).\n2453 | \n2454 | **Key obstruction**: this integral is NOT the standard positive-definite quadratic\n2455 | form `∫∫ f(g) conj(f(h)) K(g⁻¹ h) dμ dμ ≥ 0` (which follows from PD-ness of `K`).\n2456 | Instead, it is a *single* integral `∫ f(g) f(θg) K(g) dμ` with the geometric\n2457 | reflection `θ` and `K` evaluated at `g` (not `g⁻¹ h`).  PD-ness of `K` on the\n2458 | group does NOT imply this integral is non-negative; the Peter–Weyl character\n2459 | expansion of `K` and character orthogonality are needed to decompose the\n2460 | integrand into `|Fourier coefficients|²`.  See `docs/gap_analysis.md` for the\n2461 | full analysis.\n2462 | -/\n2463 | \n2464 | /-- **Clean factorization of the reflection-positivity integrand.**\n2465 | \n2466 | `osG(U) · osG(θU) = f(U) · f(θU) · exp(-β S_W(U))`.\n2467 | \n2468 | This is a purely algebraic identity: it follows from the reflection symmetries\n2469 | `S⁺(θU) = S⁻(U)` and `S_int(θU) = S_int(U)`, together with the action\n\n... 90 more line(s) below (use offset=2470 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-05 05:24:39 UTC","timestamp":1785907479,"token_count":3459,"tool_call_id":"e1ba11b9-3adb-4e79-9d56-31c263162e54","full_token_estimate":2274,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":2559,"byte_count":150137,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":10,"is_prune_marker":false}
