jobs).\",\"id\":\"74\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 21): PROVED reflection_positivity_reorganization (Step 4b of Lemma 5) + integral_matrix_element_trivial_projection. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"75\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 22): PROVED character_times_matrix_element_integral + triple_product_character_matrix_integral_timelike. Time-like triple product WITHOUT conjugation. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs). See §8.11.27.\",\"id\":\"77\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 23): ANALYZED character-level approach (§8.11.28) — does NOT directly work. KEY FINDINGS: (1) fullReflectReindex w* gives kernel |Φ_w⟩⟨Φ_{w*}| (NOT rank-1 same-vector), (2) σ twist breaks Mercer-PD structure (delta function δ(V⁰,σ(U⁰)) is discontinuous), (3) PD property of exp(-β·S_int) doesn't help because h factors break the quadratic form. CONCLUSION: L² expansion is NECESSARY. Documented in §8.11.29. Build unchanged (GREEN, 2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"76\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 24): PROVED transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect (Step 1 of Lemma 5 Step 4a). Combines Step 4e + Lemma 3 to give fullReflect form: Complex.ofReal(∫ψ·Tψ) = C·∑_w F(w)·∫ Ψ_w·A_w·A_{w*}(σ) dμ⁰. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). Also did DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization challenge (§8.11.30): c^w·c^{w*} does NOT factor as d(x)·conj(d(y)) because c^w couples i(in x) with j(in y); c^{w*}≠conj(c^w) because fullReflectReindex involves link reflection φ with selective dual; fullReflectReindex is NOT a bijection (projection losing w|_positive). Time-like case gives Tr(P^T·B_a·Q^T·B_a†) which is ≥0 iff Q=conj(P).\",\"id\":\"78\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 25): DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization (§8.11.31). KEY FINDINGS: (1) Reorganization CANNOT be done term-by-term — requires sum over w. (2) PD property of K alone does NOT imply ∫f(g)·f(g⁻¹)·K(g)≥0 — the single integral is NOT the standard PD quadratic form ∫∫f(x)·conj(f(y))·K(x⁻¹y). (3) For single time-like link, per-λ integral is NOT ≥0 (it's an inner product ⟨R,Q⟩, not a norm squared). (4) Sum over σ gives Gram matrix (PSD), but full expression couples different Fourier coefficients F_w,F_u. (5) Even/odd decomposition: I=(1/4)(∫h²·K−∫k²·K) where h=f+f∘θ (even), k=f−f∘θ (odd). (6) Non-negativity is a DEEP property requiring product structure of Boltzmann factor + support of f. (7) c^{w*}≠conj(c^w) is fundamental — σ twist breaks conjugation. MOST PROMISING ALTERNATIVE: plaquette-by-plaquette induction (approach 4) might avoid reorganization obstacle entirely. Build unchanged (GREEN, 2891 jobs).\",\"id\":\"80\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 26): KEY INSIGHT (§8.11.32) — temporal interface links are the obstacle. The reflection FIXES spatial interface links (θ(u⁰_s)=u⁰_s) but INVERTS temporal interface links (θ(w)=w⁻¹). The previous approach expanded in ALL interface links → reorganization obstacle. NEW APPROACH: expand ONLY in temporal interface links w (which are inverted), keeping spatial interface links fixed. The w-integral is a product of triple product integrals (PROVEN: triple_product_character_matrix_integral), giving Gram matrix structure with a_γ≥0. After integrating out w, the transfer matrix becomes a sum of standard integral operators in spatial links, each with Lüscher form V^{1/2}·U_γ·V^{1/2} (V=spatial plaquette factor positive, U_γ=temporal plaquette PD kernel). Each is positive, sum is positive. This AVOIDS the reorganization obstacle because: (a) spatial interface links are the SAME in both f-factors (fixed by θ), (b) the w-expansion gives Gram matrix directly via triple product integral, (c) ρ(w⁻¹)=ρ(w)† so the second f-factor's w-basis is the conjugate of the first's. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"81\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"IN PROGRESS: Lemma 5 Step 4a — NEW APPROACH (temporal interface link expansion). REMAINING STEPS: (1) Decompose interface into spatial (u⁰_s) and temporal (w) links formally, (2) Expand f in Peter-Weyl basis of w ONLY, (3) Integrate out w using triple_product_character_matrix_integral (PROVEN), (4) Show remaining operator is sum of PD kernel operators (Lüscher V^{1/2}·U·V^{1/2}), (5) Conclude ∫g·Tg≥0. See §8.11.32 for full analysis.\",\"id\":\"79\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"PENDING: Assemble lemma 6 — close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (axiom count 6→5). See §8.8. Requires Lemma 5 Step 4a (item 79).\",\"id\":\"48\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}","name":"project_task_list"},"id":"a1eeb83c-226e-4e31-988a-041a90d53b7d","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":1854,"reasoning_content":"I'm at 88% context. Let me update the project task list and prepare for handoff. I need to:\n1. Update project_task_list with the new findings\n2. Update todo_list\n3. Handoff with a clear next_prompt\n\nLet me update the project task list first.","turn":29,"is_prune_marker":false}
