{"id":54,"role":"Assistant","content":"","timestamp":1785909449,"token_count":0,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"reason\":\"Context at 90%. Session 26 completed deep analysis identifying the key mathematical insight (temporal interface links are the obstacle) and a clear path forward. No code changes this session — pure analysis documented in §8.11.32. Build is GREEN (2891 jobs). Next session should begin implementing the new approach.\",\"next_prompt\":\"You are continuing the YangMills Lean 4 formalization project (goal: close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`, axiom count 6→5). Read `project_task_list` first.\\n\\n## Current state (session 26 → 27)\\n\\n**BUILD IS GREEN** (2891 jobs). All code compiles. 0 sorries, 0 new custom axioms. No code changes were made in session 26 — it was pure mathematical analysis.\\n\\n### What was done in session 26\\n\\nSession 26 identified the **KEY MATHEMATICAL INSIGHT** that unblocks the proof. This is documented in `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` §8.11.32 (appended at the end of the file, starting at line ~2594).\\n\\n**The core insight: TEMPORAL INTERFACE LINKS are the obstacle.**\\n\\nThe reflection θ acts differently on the two types of interface links (links at sites with signedTime=0):\\n- **Spatial interface links** U((0,x), i): θ maps to U((0,x), i) — **FIXED** (same site, spatial direction, no inverse)\\n- **Temporal interface links** U((0,x), 0) = w(x): θ maps to U((0,x), 0)⁻¹ = w(x)⁻¹ — **INVERTED**\\n\\nThis was confirmed by reading `reflectLinkVariable` (Lattice.lean:198) and `reflectToPosInterface` (TransferMatrix.lean:1111).\\n\\n**Why the previous approach (§8.11.30-31) failed:** It expanded f in the Peter-Weyl basis of ALL interface links (both spatial and temporal). The spatial and temporal links have different reflection behavior, so the coefficients c^w and c^{w*} couldn't be related by conjugation, leading to the reorganization obstacle.\\n\\n**The NEW approach (§8.11.32):** Expand f in the Peter-Weyl basis of the TEMPORAL interface links w ONLY, keeping the spatial interface links u⁰_s fixed (since they're fixed by θ). This works because:\\n1. The spatial interface links are the SAME in both f-factors (fixed by θ), so no mismatch there.\\n2. The temporal interface links w are inverted by θ, so ρ(w⁻¹) = ρ(w)† — the second f-factor's w-basis functions are conjugates of the first's.\\n3. The integral over w of `Φ_α(w) · conj(Φ_β(w)) · exp(-β·S_ts_upper(w))` is a PRODUCT of triple product integrals (one per spatial site x), each handled by the PROVEN lemma `triple_product_character_matrix_integral` (PeterWeyl.lean:1740).\\n4. The triple product integral gives a **Gram matrix structure**: `M_{α,β} = ∑_γ P_γ(α)·conj(P_γ(β))·a_γ` where a_γ ≥ 0 (plaquette factor coefficients from `plaquetteBoltzmannPD`).\\n5. After integrating out w, the transfer matrix becomes a sum of standard integral operators in the spatial links, each with the **Lüscher form** V^{1/2}·U_γ·V^{1/2} (V = spatial plaquette factor, positive multiplication; U_γ = temporal plaquette operator, PD kernel in spatial links). Each is positive, so the sum is positive.\\n\\n### The interface action decomposition (key for the proof)\\n\\nFrom `wilsonActionOSInterface` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:455), the interface action decomposes as:\\n- `S_spatial_0(u⁰_s)`: pure spatial plaquettes at t=0 (interface only, reflection-invariant, depends on u⁰_s only)\\n- `S_ts_upper(u⁺, u⁰_s, w)`: time-space plaquettes at t=0 (involve positive links + temporal interface w + spatial interface u⁰_s)\\n- `S_ts_lower(U⁻, u⁰_s)`: time-space plaquettes at t=-1 (involve negative links + spatial interface u⁰_s, **NOT w**)\\n\\nKey: **w appears ONLY in S_ts_upper and in f — NOT in S_ts_lower.** This means the integral over U⁻ (negative links) is independent of w, allowing the factorization.\\n\\n### The clear path forward (NEW PLAN — item 79 in project_task_list)\\n\\n1. **Decompose interface into spatial (u⁰_s) and temporal (w) links.** Define the split formally in Lean. The interface sites have signedTime=0; links at these sites in direction μ=0 are temporal (w), in direction μ≠0 are spatial (u⁰_s).\\n\\n2. **Expand f in Peter-Weyl basis of w ONLY.** Write `f(U⁺, u⁰_s, w) = ∑_α c_α(U⁺, u⁰_s) · Φ_α(w)` where Φ_α = ∏_x (ρ_{λ_x}(w_x))_{i_x,j_x} are the Peter-Weyl basis functions of the product group SU(N)^n (n = number of spatial sites at t=0).\\n\\n3. **Integrate out w using the triple product integral** (PROVEN: `triple_product_character_matrix_integral`). The integral `∫ Φ_α(w) · conj(Φ_β(w)) · exp(-β·S_ts_upper(w)) dw` factorizes as a product over spatial sites x, each being a triple product integral. This gives the Gram matrix structure with a_γ ≥ 0.\\n\\n4. **Show the remaining operator is a sum of PD kernel operators** (Lüscher decomposition). After integrating out w, the transfer matrix is a sum over γ of integral operators in the spatial links, each with kernel K_γ(U⁺, U⁻, u⁰_s). Each K_γ has the Lüscher form: V^{1/2} (spatial plaquette factor, positive multiplication) · U_γ (temporal plaquette PD kernel) · V^{1/2}. Each term is positive because U_γ is PD (from `plaquetteBoltzmannPD`) and V is positive.\\n\\n5. **Conclude `∫ g·Tg ≥ 0`** from the positivity of the sum of positive operators. This closes `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`.\\n\\n### Key concern to verify in the next session\\n\\nThe plaquette factor coefficients a_γ(U⁺, u⁰_s) depend on U⁺ (through the matrix elements (ρ_ν(A_x))_{qp} where A_x is the product of the other 3 links in the upper interface plaquette). If a_γ is NOT constant in U⁺, the non-negativity requires showing that a_γ · exp(-β·S_pos) is the full positive Boltzmann factor (which is PD). This needs careful verification — see Finding 7 in §8.11.32.\\n\\n### Key files & line numbers\\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PeterWeyl.lean`: `triple_product_character_matrix_integral` (1740, WITH conjugation — this is the one needed for the w-expansion since ρ(w⁻¹)=ρ(w)† gives the conjugation), `triple_product_character_matrix_integral_timelike` (2060, WITHOUT conjugation), `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` (search for it — gives a_γ ≥ 0), `reflection_positivity_reorganization` (1702), axiom `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` (226).\\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/TransferMatrix.lean`: `transferMatrixCorrect` (1279, the transfer matrix to decompose), `reflectToPosInterface` (1111, confirms θ(u⁰) inverts temporal interface links), `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (4776, the key identity ∫G·G(θU) = ∫g·Tg), `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect` (5632).\\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean`: `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (2341, the axiom to close), `interfaceSites` (203, signedTime=0), `wilsonActionOSInterface` (455, the interface action to decompose), `positiveSites`/`negativeSites` (191/197).\\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Lattice.lean`: `reflectLinkVariable` (198, the reflection: temporal links inverted, spatial links fixed).\\n- `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md`: §8.11.32 (THIS SESSION's key insight — the full analysis).\\n\\n### Build commands\\n- Windows build: `powershell -Command \\\"lake build YangMills.Proofs.TransferMatrix 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\\\"`\\n- Full build: `powershell -Command \\\"lake build 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\\\"`\\n\\n### Suggested first action for session 27\\n1. Read §8.11.32 in the design doc for the full analysis.\\n2. Start by formally decomposing the interface links into spatial (u⁰_s) and temporal (w) components. This requires defining a function that splits `interfaceSites` links by direction (μ=0 → temporal, μ≠0 → spatial).\\n3. Then define the Peter-Weyl expansion of f in the w variables and set up the triple product integral application.\\n4. The triple product integral lemma is already proven — the main work is in the setup (decomposition, expansion, factorization) and the final assembly (Lüscher decomposition → positivity).\"}","name":"handoff"},"id":"5f7187b9-abcf-436c-979b-faafc937a689","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":1648,"reasoning_content":"I'm at 90% context. I need to handoff now. Let me prepare a comprehensive handoff.","turn":31,"is_prune_marker":false}
